<section class="enq-missed-call" aria-labelledby="enq-missed-call-title">
  <div class="container enq-missed-call__grid">
    <div class="enq-missed-call__copy">
      <p class="product-kicker product-kicker--light">Missed calls</p>
      <h2 id="enq-missed-call-title">A missed call doesn't have to mean a missed customer.</h2>
      <p>You might be serving one customer when another one calls. Chakusa turns that missed call into a visible lead, with the time it came in attached, so it's still there to follow up on, not just a notification that disappeared from your screen.</p>
      <p>On Android, this happens on its own once you turn on the Recovery Engine permission, using only the phone number and time of the call, never call recordings or your address book. Every follow-up after that, preparing a message, marking it contacted, is still something you choose to do.</p>
      <p class="enq-missed-call__note">Chakusa doesn't promise a missed call becomes revenue. It promises the call doesn't just disappear.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="enq-missed-call__visual" role="img" aria-label="A missed call becomes a lead ready for follow-up">
      <div class="enq-call-flow" aria-hidden="true"><span>Missed call</span><i></i><span>New lead</span><i></i><span>Follow up</span></div>
      <strong>One missed call. One clear next action.</strong>
      <small>The lead stays visible until the business responds.</small>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
